					<h1 class="title" title="Union Territories">Union Territories</h1>
					<div class="entry-content">

                <a href="Union-Territories/Andaman-and-Nicobar.aspx"><strong>Andaman and Nicobar</strong></a>
<p>Andaman and Nicobar is a lovely place to visit with so many things to see. There are around 500 islands spreading across the total distance of 780 Kms. The Andaman groups of islands are originally populated by the Great Andamanese, the Onge, the Jarawa and the Sentinelese. Port Blair is the capital of Andaman and Nicobar. The Andaman and  Nicobar islands are renowned for the pristine clean coral beaches.                 </p>
<a href="Union-Territories/Dadar-and-Nagar-Haveli.aspx"><strong>Dadar & Nagar Haveli</strong></a>
                <p>Gifted with nature's bounty, it's a land of spell-binding beauty lush green forests, winding rivers, unimaginable waterfronts, gentle gurgle of streams, distant dotting mountain ranges, a gorgeous kaleidoscope of flora and fauna Owing to its tranquility and quaint sylvan surroundings, this territory is a heaven for those who hunt around for a tranquil holiday. </p>
                
                <a href="Union-Territories/Daman-and-Diu.aspx"><strong>Daman and Diu</strong></a>
<p>Daman & Diu is the second smallest Union Territory of India, located on the west coast. It spreads to only 122 square kms. This coastal enclave has two districts- Diu and Daman.</p>
                <a href="Union-Territories/Lakshadweep.aspx"><strong>Lakshadweep</strong></a>
<p>The amazingly beautiful Lakshadweep is a group of 36 small Islands in the Arabian Sea. It is the smallest Union Territory of India. The charming Lakshadweep is densely covered with coconut palms and is serenely set in aquamarine sea.</p>
                <a href="Union-Territories/Puducherry.aspx"><strong>Puducherry</strong></a>
<p>The small and serene city Pondicherry is situated on the Coromandel Coast, established by the French. Pondicherry includes three different cities of three different states, namely Karaikal (Tamil Nadu), Mahe (Kerala), and Yanam (Andhra Pradesh). The natural scenic beauty of Deccan plateau is witnessed on the way to Pondicherry. The deep green vegetation in striking red soil forms a stunning landscape. </p>
&nbsp;</div> <!-- end .entry-content -->
